1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,000
Along the gentle curve of the Chao Phraya River, the historic story of Bangkok began as a bustling trading post.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:16,500
In 1782, King Rama I established his new royal capital on Rattanakosin Island, founding the Chakri dynasty.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Within protective river moats rose the Grand Palace and Wat Phra Kaew, enshrining the sacred Emerald Buddha.

4
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:33,500
Nearby, the ancient temple of Wat Pho safeguarded classical Buddhist scriptures, medicine, and monastic arts.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Across the river in Thonburi, the porcelain-encrusted central spire of Wat Arun rose high into the morning sky.

6
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:50,500
Throughout the centuries, intricate canal networks transformed the capital into the vibrant Venice of the East.

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,500
From royal citadel to thriving modern metropolis, Bangkok endures as an immortal city along the River of Kings.
